><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name><name><surname>Schnapp</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Block</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Direct observation of kinesin stepping by optical trapping interferometry</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1993</year><volume>365</volume><fpage>721</fpage><lpage>727</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/365721a0</pub-id><!-- WARNING: Occurrence has not been converted --></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Svoboda K, Schmidt CF, Schnapp BJ, Block SM (1993) Direct observation of kinesin stepping by optical trapping interferometry. Nature 365:721&#x02013;727 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8413650</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Valentine</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Fordyce</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Krzysiak</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilbert</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Block</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Individual dimers of the mitotic kinesin motor Eg5 step processively and support substantial loads in vitro</article-title><source>Nat Cell Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>470</fpage><lpage>476</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/ncb1394</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Valentine MT, Fordyce PM, Krzysiak TC, Gilbert SP, Block SM (2006) Individual dimers of the mitotic kinesin motor Eg5 step processively and support substantial loads in vitro. Nat Cell Biol 8:470&#x02013;476 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16604065</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>Mikhail J. Korneev and Stefan Lak&#x000e4;mper have contributed equally to this work.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>